  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Movie Library System (MUM Senior Project)",
    "description": "I developed a web application, where users were able to see general information about movies, they could also make comments and rate the movie they choose. There was a registration process with email confirmation in which the user needed to provide a code sent to his/her email before he login into the site for first time (this corresponded to an activation page). The main modules of the application were: Login, Register, account activation, and managed movies (add, delete, update, and search for a movie). Some of the technologies used in this project were: PHP, Javascript, HTML5, CSS3, AJAX, and MySQL Database.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Nov 2014 - Dec 2014"
   },
   {
    "title": "Online Yoga Studio System",
    "description": "Worked as part of a team of fellow undergraduate students to design a Java web application for an online yoga studio. The project included a schedule of classes and a system for registering for and managing classes and faculty, complete with prerequisite checking and a waiver system. The app was built in Java EE7, JavaServer Faces 2.2. Software analysis and design was done primarily in Star UML. My part in the project was to build front end pages with HTML, CSS and JSF, as well as handling the OOAD for several use cases.\n",
